--- cleanup ---
demo servers killed by PID; marker file removed

--- 3. code execution at unpickle time (logged honestly) ---
The evil-cookie request returned HTTP 400 (the handler does data['user'] on the
unpickle result, and the __reduce__ payload returned int 0 from os.system -> TypeError).
BUT the marker file /tmp/deserwalk/PWNED-marker existed afterward (verified with
ls -la, timestamped during the run): os.system ran INSIDE pickle.loads, before the
application ever touched the result. The 400 is the app choking on the return value;
the execution had already happened. This ordering - code runs during parsing,
before application logic - is the lesson's core mechanism, demonstrated.
(marker file removed after verification)
